# What `releng` carries that a medium whose only job is to install this system
# does not need, one per line. Removing them is worth about 120 MiB of
# packages, which is not what decides the size of the image; it is worth doing
# because a medium that only installs should not carry another installer, a web
# server, four VPN clients and three filesystem toolsets this project never
# touches. Less on it is less to explain and less to go wrong.
#
# What is deliberately kept, because it is a judgement and not an obvious cut:
# `lvm2` and `mdadm`, for a disk that arrives that way; `vim` and `nano`, for
# when something has to be looked at; `tmux`, `openssh`, `rsync`, `usbutils`,
# `dmidecode` and the TPM tools. And `zsh` with `grml-zsh-config`, which are not
# optional at all: `releng` gives root a zsh, and a medium whose root has no
# shell does not log in.

# Another installer
archinstall

# Serving, scanning and talking to the network in ways an installation does not
darkhttpd
dnsmasq
bind
ldns
lftp
ndisc6
nmap
openconnect
openvpn
pptpclient
vpnc
wvdial
xl2tpd
ppp
linux-atm
modemmanager
usb_modeswitch
usbmuxd

# Cloning and rescuing disks
clonezilla
partclone
partimage
fsarchiver
testdisk
ddrescue
gpart

# Filesystems this project does not lay down
xfsprogs
jfsutils
nilfs-utils
f2fs-tools
exfatprogs
ntfsprogs
udftools
bcachefs-tools
dmraid

# Guests of hypervisors this medium is not a guest of
open-vm-tools
qemu-guest-agent
virtualbox-guest-utils-nox
hyperv

# Sound, speech and braille, which an installer does not use
alsa-utils
sof-firmware
espeakup
brltty
livecd-sounds

# The rest
cloud-init
mc
irssi
lynx
screen
gpm
hdparm
sdparm
